    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1101">

                <pb facs="1161" n="1041" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg1041"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.679 Residence and Establishment/72:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-28T13:00:00+02:00">August 28, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 28—10:50 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>34. Department’s 28, July 27, 11 a.m., and No. 320, February 26.<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d1101-f1"/> The treaty, with the preamble which the Department
                    preferred, was initialed yesterday. The proceedings are confidential. The
                    assurances (see “Annex D” of Department’s No. 320) were not given because they
                    were not requested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
